From 9881f51d70626978659a43a052e29afd35a9ebbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:23:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 099/109] fix(classifier): confine manifest.json and keep
 failed image declarations out of the text layout

Review round 1 of B204 found three ways the shared layout detector could
misread a model directory, on all three engines:

- manifest.json was opened, through any symlink, before any confinement
  check. It now has to resolve inside the model dir (or its registry
  repository) before it is read, and the read is bounded to 1 MiB.
- A manifest declaring "task": "image-classification" whose labels_file
  failed a check (absolute, "..", empty, not a string) fell through to the
  text layout when tokenizer.json and config.json were present, so et and ort
  loaded an explicit image model as a text classifier. The declaration is now
  tri-state: absent, valid, or invalid, and invalid is no layout. A manifest
  that cannot be read safely (escaping link, oversized, not a JSON object)
  is no layout either, because what it declares is unknown.
- The confinement root widened to the parent of any ancestor named
  "snapshots". It now widens only for a snapshots dir directly under a
  registry repository (models--*, modelscope--models--*).

An engine that predates image classification answers 404 on
/classify/image; that 404 is now a 502 image_classification_unsupported
naming the first release that serves the route (tflite-server 0.2.0,
et-server 0.2.0, ort-server 0.2.0-musl). The load mismatch error reads
"needs the <layout> layout, but '<dir>' has the <layout> layout" (or "has no
servable classifier layout"), and a backend with nothing loaded says so on
either route.

test_classifier_layout covers every case above for tflite, executorch and
onnxruntime through the detector, each recipe's resolver and the load
check. server_image_classify.py adds test_517 (an engine without the image
route, through the fake's FAKE_NO_IMAGE_ROUTE) and test_518 (invalid image
declarations and an escaping manifest link never load).

